    {
      "id": 12687,
      "name": "Trajector",
      "username": "Trajector",
      "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/trajector/{size}/1914_2.png",
      "created_at": "2015-03-19T03:37:57.000Z",
      "cooked": "<p>Some cards mention powers that deal damage. For instance, Unity's Hasty Augmentation or the title Living Weapon. In most cases it's clear what they mean but what about when a power lets a hero play a card, and then that card deals damage?&nbsp;</p><p>For example, suppose Unity plays Hasty Augmentation, and then lets Omnitron-X use a power. Omnitron-X Timeshifts itself, revealing Sedative Flechettes. Do the&nbsp;<span>Flechettes do 2 damage, because the damage comes from playing the card, or 4 damage, because playing the card was part of using a power? </span></p><p><span>More complicated still, what if Omnitron-X Timeshifts Ra, who reveals a Fire Blast? Or if it Timeshifts Wraith, who reveals an Impromptu Invention and uses THAT to play a Throat Jab? In some sense, all of the events trace back to Omnitron-X's power. But in another sense, each new card seems like a new source.</span></p><p><span>Is there an unambiguous answer?&nbsp;</span></p>",
      "post_number": 1,
      "post_type": 1,
      "updated_at": "2021-02-07T01:44:17.679Z",
      "reply_count": 0,
      "reply_to_post_number": null,
      "quote_count": 0,
      "incoming_link_count": 0,
      "reads": 0,
      "readers_count": 0,
      "score": 0.0,
      "yours": false,
      "topic_id": 12685,
      "topic_slug": "can-powers-that-play-cards-deal-damage",
